# JavaScript Development

## Code Organization

**Separate files by feature** (not one monolithic file):

- `js/jquery.main.js` - Main theme functionality and Fancybox init
- `js/background-sections.js` - Scroll-driven background system
- `js/block-styles.js` - Gutenberg editor enhancements

**Each feature gets its own file** when adding new functionality.

## Vanilla JS (ES5+ Compatible)

**Use IIFE** to avoid global scope pollution:

```javascript
(function () {
  'use strict';
  
  // Your code here
  function init() {
    // Initialization
  }
  
  // DOM ready
  if (document.readyState === "loading") {
    document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", init);
  } else {
    init();
  }
})();
```

## Naming Conventions

**Variables/Functions**: camelCase

```javascript
const bgEl = document.getElementById("site-bg");
const activeLayer = layers[nextKey];
let transitionInProgress = false;

function getVariantFromEl(el) { }
function beginVariantTransition(bgEl, layers, nextVariant) { }
```

**Constants**: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE

```javascript
const TRANSITION_MS = 900;
const VARIANTS = [
  { slug: "yellow", label: "Yellow" },
  // ...
];
```

## jQuery Usage

- jQuery available (WordPress core dependency)
- Use `jQuery` or pass `$` to IIFE:

```javascript
jQuery(function($) {
  // $ is safe inside this scope
  $('.element').on('click', function() { });
});
```

## Fancybox Integration

**In `js/jquery.main.js`**:

```javascript
Fancybox.bind("[data-fancybox]", {
  // Configuration options
});
```

**In HTML** (blocks/templates):

```html
<button data-fancybox data-src="#modal-id">Open Modal</button>
```

## Gutenberg Editor JavaScript

**In `js/block-styles.js`**:

```javascript
/* global wp */
(function () {
  if (!window.wp) return;
  
  const { addFilter } = wp.hooks;
  const { createHigherOrderComponent } = wp.compose;
  // ... Gutenberg APIs
})();
```

**For block styles registration**:

```javascript
wp.domReady(function () {
  if (wp.blocks && wp.blocks.registerBlockStyle) {
    wp.blocks.registerBlockStyle("core/group", {
      name: "background-section",
      label: "Background section"
    });
  }
});
```

## DOM Selectors

**Prefer data attributes** for JS hooks:

```javascript
// Good - semantic, clear purpose
document.querySelector('[data-fancybox]');
document.querySelectorAll('[data-bg-variant]');

// Avoid - couples JS to styling
document.querySelector('.btn-primary');
```

## Performance Considerations

**Use Intersection Observer** (not scroll events):

```javascript
const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
  (entries) => {
    entries.forEach((entry) => {
      if (entry.isIntersecting) {
        // Handle intersection
      }
    });
  },
  {
    root: null,
    rootMargin: "-30% 0px -30% 0px",
    threshold: [0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1]
  }
);

sections.forEach((el) => observer.observe(el));
```

**Check for prefers-reduced-motion**:

```javascript
function prefersReducedMotion() {
  return window.matchMedia && 
         window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches;
}

if (prefersReducedMotion()) {
  // Disable or simplify animations
}
```

## No Magic Numbers

```javascript
// ❌ Bad
setTimeout(callback, 900);
rootMargin: "-30% 0px -30% 0px"

// ✅ Good
const TRANSITION_MS = 900;
const INTERSECTION_MARGIN = "-30% 0px -30% 0px";

setTimeout(callback, TRANSITION_MS);
rootMargin: INTERSECTION_MARGIN
```

## Creating Public APIs (If Needed)

**Namespace under theme object**:

```javascript
window.curixusTheme = window.curixusTheme || {};

window.curixusTheme.bgSections = {
  getVariant: getVariantFromEl,
  setVariant: function(variant) { /* ... */ }
};
```

**Document any public API** in code comments.

## Enqueuing JavaScript

**In `inc/scripts.php`** ONLY:

```php
wp_enqueue_script( 
  'custom', 
  get_template_directory_uri() . '/js/custom.js', 
  array('jquery'), // Dependencies
  filemtime(get_template_directory() . '/js/custom.js'),
  true // In footer
);
```

